lable Positions Open theÂ Employment Position Application Â feature. ClickÂ Search positions . Tip You can narrow your search by entering text in any of the filters. Then clickÂ Search positions . The fewer criteria selected, the more results the search returns. The search only retrieves active positions that fit your combined selection requirements. To view all open positions, do not specify any search criteria and click theÂ Search positions Â button. In the search results, click on a position title to view a detailed job description, access the online application form, and submit additional attachments such as your resume and references. Once you start filling out the online application, the system guides you through the application process. Complete an Online Application In the Employment Position Application feature, search for positions. From the search results, click on the position title to which you want to apply. The full job description appears. ClickÂ Apply Now Â orÂ Apply for the Position Title . TheÂ Employment ApplicationÂ page appears. Click Click here to start filling out this employment application Â link. TheÂ Personal InformationÂ page of the application appears. Enter your personal information, and clickÂ Next Page Â to continue with the online application. Online applications may vary by position. Tip At any time during the application process, you can save your current progress and complete the application at another time by clicking theÂ Save and Finish LaterÂ button. You are provided a login key that allows you to retrieve and complete your application. To easily access the same position, bookmark the page. For detailed procedures on completing a saved application, see Complete a Saved Application. When you have successfully completed the online application, theÂ Review and SubmitÂ page appears. Review your application carefully. If updates need to be made to the application, click theÂ Previous Page Â orÂ View Table of Contents Â link to access the sections requiring an update. If the application is ready to be submitted, click theÂ Submit Application Â button. TheÂ Application InformationÂ page appears. To upload a document related to your application such as a copy of your resume or cover letter: Note The documents that can be uploaded and submitted with an application vary by position and in some instances may not be a part of the application process at all. Click theÂ Upload yourÂ file Â link. TheÂ Upload a FileÂ window appears. Click theÂ Choose File Â button. TheÂ OpenÂ window appears. Browse to the location of the file you want to upload. Select it and click theÂ OpenÂ button. TheÂ OpenÂ window closes, and the selected file appears on theÂ Upload a FileÂ window. Click theÂ SaveÂ button. TheÂ Upload a FileÂ window closes. Tip To delete an uploaded document, click theÂ Trash canÂ icon. TheÂ UploadÂ option reappears. To enter your information related to your application online: Note The text that can be entered and submitted with an application varies by position and in some instances may not be a part of the application process at all. Click theÂ Enter as TextÂ link. Enter or copy and paste your information in the text box. Note When text is pasted into the text box, any formatting is lost. Click theÂ SaveÂ button. Tip To delete entered text, click theÂ Trash canÂ icon. TheÂ Enter as textÂ option reappears. Your application is submitted to the HR Department. Once it has been reviewed, you will receive a login that allows you to return to the site and check the application status. Complete My Saved Application Access the bookmarked page or use the search options to locate the position to which you started the online application,Â and clickÂ Apply Now Â orÂ Apply for the Position Title . TheÂ Employment ApplicationÂ page appears. From theÂ Retrieve a Saved Employment Application Â section, enter the key provided or sent to you in an email when you saved the application. Click theÂ Retrieve Employment Application Â button. The online application appears. Use theÂ Next Page Â andÂ Previous Page Â links to browse through the online application, or click theÂ View Table of ContentsÂ link to quickly access a specific section. Update or complete any additional application information. When you have successfully completed the online application, theÂ Review and SubmitÂ page appears. Review your application carefully. If updates need to be made to the application, click theÂ Previous Page Â orÂ View Table of Contents Â link to access the sections requiring an update. If the application is ready to be submitted, click theÂ Submit Application Â button. TheÂ Application InformationÂ page appears. To upload a document related to your application such as a copy of your resume or cover letter: Note The documents that can be uploaded and submitted with an application vary by position and in some instances may not be a part of the application process at all. Click theÂ Upload yourÂ file Â link. TheÂ Upload a FileÂ window appears. Click theÂ Choose File Â button. TheÂ OpenÂ window appears. Browse to the location of the file you want to upload. Select it, and click theÂ OpenÂ button. TheÂ OpenÂ window closes, and the selected file appears on theÂ Upload a FileÂ window. Click theÂ SaveÂ button. TheÂ Upload a FileÂ window closes. Tip To delete an uploaded document, click theÂ Trash canÂ icon. TheÂ UploadÂ option reappears. To enter your information online: Note The text that can be entered and submitted with an application varies by position and in some instances may not be a part of the application process at all. Click theÂ Enter as Text Â link. Â Enter or copy and paste your information in the text box. Note When text is pasted into the text box, any formatting is lost. Click theÂ SaveÂ button. Tip To delete entered text, click theÂ Trash canÂ icon. TheÂ Enter as textÂ option reappears. Your application is submitted to the HR Department. Once it has been reviewed, you will receive a login that allows you to return to the site and check the application status. Find out Whether Your Online Application Was Submitted Successfully Complete the online application process. You will receive an email confirmation that the HR Administrator has accepted your application. Using the log in and key provided in your email confirmation, log back in. View the status of your application, and double-check the information you submitted. Contact Someone Regarding a Position You can email a designated point of contact for a specific position to get more information, notify of them technical difficulties, or verify your submission. Access the position's bookmarked page or use the search options to locate the position for which you want to contact someone. From theÂ Employment ApplicationÂ page, clickÂ Ask us a question . A blank email in your default email client such as Outlook or Exchange automatically appears. Enter your email content and make any necessary updates to theÂ Subject,Â CC, orÂ BCCÂ fields. Click theÂ SendÂ button. Your email is sent to the point of contact for the selected position. View Your Application Status Log in to the Campus Portal using the user name and password you received in the application confirmation email. Access theÂ Employment Position Application Â page. TheÂ Your recent applicationsÂ section displays all the positions to which you have applied and their current status. To view more information, click on a specific position title. TheÂ Position Details Â page appears. To view your complete online application, clickÂ View your application . TheÂ Application DetailsÂ page appears. To view theÂ Position DetailsÂ page, clickÂ Return to previous screen. Tip Status Descriptions Being Reviewed : Your resume was successfully submitted and has been entered into applicant pool for the position. Your application will be reviewed for a potential match between department's hiring needs and candidate's qualifications for position. Approved for an Interview : The hiring committee is interested in interviewing you for the position and will contact you directly or has already contacted you. Your application was declined : You are no longer being considered for the open position. Decisions are based on the department's hiring needs and preferences and candidate's qualifications for the position. Your application was withdrawn : You no longer wish to be considered for the open position. View All Your Applications You can keep track of all the positions to which you have applied. To easily access the same position, bookmark the page. Log in to the Campus Portal using the user name and password you received in the application confirmation email. Access theÂ Employment ApplicationÂ page. TheÂ Your recent applications Â section displays all the positions to which you have applied and their current status. To view more information, click on a specific position title. TheÂ Position DetailsÂ page appears. Withdraw My Application If for some reason you must withdraw your application, you can log in and remove your application from consideration. Note Once an application has been withdrawn, it cannot be reinstated. Log in to the Campus Portal using the user name and password you received in the application confirmation email. Access theÂ Employment ApplicationÂ page. TheÂ Your recent applications Â section displays all the positions to which you have applied and their current status. Click on a title of the position to which you have applied and from which want to withdraw your application. TheÂ Position DetailsÂ page appears. ClickÂ Withdraw your application for this position . Your application is automatically withdrawn for consideration. Related Topics Employment Position Application Setup Employment Position Application How To Search for Available Positions Complete an Online Application Complete My Saved Application Find out Whether Your Online Application Was Submitted Successfully Contact Someone Regardin